      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.08,
      "end_seconds": 272.23,
      "duration_seconds": 17.15,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like stable recovery after the heart event. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'll request a lipid profile, it'll help with cardiovascular risk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.18,
      "end_seconds": 275.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.57,
      "end_seconds": 302.26,
      "duration_seconds": 25.69,
      "text": "I'm going to put you on atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night, long term. You take it by mouth. That's for cardiovascular risk. Cardiac rehab is worth doing, it really helps your confidence. I'll also refer you to cardiac rehabilitation. An ECG is something we might do if this doesn't improve in a month. What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.03,
      "end_seconds": 309.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "So, I take the atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.01,
      "end_seconds": 315.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's all. Go gently."
    },
